  "title": "Matchsticks to Square",
  "summary": "Given an integer array matchsticks, where each element represents the length of a matchstick, determine if it's possible to form a square using all matchsticks exactly once without breaking any.",
  "statement": "Given an integer array matchsticks, where each element represents the length of a matchstick, determine if it's possible to form a square using all matchsticks exactly once without breaking any. Return true if possible, otherwise false.",
  "constraints": [
    "1 <= matchsticks.length <= 15; 1 <= each length <= 100,000,000.",
    "Use every stick exactly once to form four equal sides. Sticks may be joined but never broken.",
    "Return a boolean. Divisibility of the total by four is necessary, not sufficient."
  ],
