  "hints": [
    "After checking divisibility, the target side length is total/4.",
    "Place longer sticks first and recursively try every side that has enough remaining capacity.",
    "After placing a stick, recurse on the next index; undo failed choices. Equal side totals are interchangeable.",
    "Memoize the next index and sorted side totals to merge symmetric states. Using every stick under four capacity limits forces equality."
  ],
  "editorial": "Each complete assignment is a partition of sticks into four side buckets. Exhaustively trying feasible buckets preserves all solutions; sorting and symmetry reduce repeated work but do not make a greedy commitment. The independent oracle instead builds subset masks that complete one side before starting another. This is four-way partition, not the existing two-way equal-subset problem.",
